+Upgrade and restore candidates use the same serialized migration executor. The pre-047/048 preservation hook and migration 052 keep checkpoint, exact history and inferred furthest evidence distinct. See `../recovery/READING_UPGRADE.md`.
 
-## Teardown behavior
+The source operator restore entry point remains `scripts/backup/postgres-restore.sh` with its existing explicit confirmation. It now resolves the same host-local root before invoking the same agent. Old bare-filename selectors, deployment quiescence/restart, operation reconciliation, pins, generation fencing, NAS reference validation and full dump/snapshot restore still require combined qualification. Do not infer production readiness from a visible Restore button or a source check.
 
-Normal `./hybrid-down.sh` preserves `mreader_backup_spool` and all NAS backups. A full local purge can delete the local spool, but MReader hybrid teardown never deletes the NAS backup namespace.
+Secure browser download delivery is unfinished and remains disabled. The private admin API has no verified streaming transport to the host-local owner yet. It must not expose the recovery root through the public media service or silently return to NAS downloads. The existing namespace-secret construction also needs narrowing before introducing an export credential.
